<p>The post <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com/madonnas-like-a-prayer-turns-27-today/20160321">Madonna’s Like A Prayer turns 27 today.</a> appeared first on <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com">Madonna news new album Rebel Heart</a>.</p>
]]></description>
				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<h4>That’s right. 27. And its songs are still iconic…</h4>
<p>You’re probably feeling rather old right now, but don’t worry about that. Like a fine wine, you and <strong>Like a Prayer</strong> have simply gotten better with age.</p>
<p>To celebrate,<strong> <a href="https://www.gaytimes.co.uk/culture/31586/madonnas-like-prayer-turns-27-today/" target="_blank">Gay Times</a></strong> have 14 Like a Prayer facts for you:</p>
<p><strong>01.</strong> The Vatican predictably condemned the video for Like a Prayer, because of all of the religious themes. You could easily do a fun countdown of all the things that offended them.</p>
<p><strong>02.</strong> The imagery and lyrics for Like a Prayer were inspired by Madonna’s Catholic upbringing</p>
<p><strong>03.</strong> Prince played guitar on three songs from the album, including Like a Prayer.</p>
<p><strong>04.</strong> Like a Prayer was of course Madonna’s fourth studio album.</p>
<p><strong>05.</strong> On the controversy over the religious imagery, Madonna told the New York Times in 1989: “Art should be controversial and that’s all there is to it.”</p>
<p><strong>06.</strong> The album was top of the Billboard charts for <strong>six</strong> weeks.</p>
<p><strong>07.</strong> Like a Prayer, the single, was Madonna’s seventh number one single on the Billboard Hot 100</p>
<p><strong>08.</strong> Taylor Swift told Kiss FM that on this album Madonna made “the most incredible, bold, risky, decisions as far as pop music goes.”</p>
<p><strong>09.</strong> Taylor also called the title track “legitimately one of the greatest pop songs of all time”.</p>
<p><strong>10.</strong> Madonna talked about her relationship with her family on songs like Keep it Together and Oh Father. She had just turned 30, the age her mother died, so wanted to explore family on the album.</p>
<p><strong>11.</strong> The album was a comeback after the relative lack of success of her film Who’s That Girl in 1987 and her divorce from Sean Penn in 1989.</p>
<p><strong>12. </strong>Mary Lambert directed the Like a Prayer video. She worked with Madonna multiple times, including the videos for Like a Virgin and Material Girl.</p>
<p><strong>13.</strong> Madonna starred on Broadway in a show called Speed-the-Plow during production of the album.</p>
<p><strong>14.</strong> The second single off the album, Express Yourself, has long been an anthem for empowering women.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Keep on reading: <strong><a href="https://www.gaytimes.co.uk/culture/31586/madonnas-like-prayer-turns-27-today/" target="_blank">Gay Times</a>.</strong></p>
